        <h2>Purpose</h2>
        <p>
            This application is used solely for
            personal backup operations between
            a privately operated Linux server
            and the owner's Google Drive account.
        </p>

        <h2>Information Accessed</h2>
        <p>
            The application uses Google OAuth 2.0
            authentication to access Google Drive
            files and folders for backup and
            synchronisation purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
        <p>
            Google Drive data is accessed only
            to perform the owner's requested
            backup and synchronisation tasks.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>
        <p>
            Authentication credentials are stored
            locally on the owner's Linux server.
            They are not published or shared
            with third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>
            This application is not a public
            service. Google user data is not
            sold or shared with advertisers
            or unrelated third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>
            Backup files remain in the owner's
            Google Drive account until they are
            removed through the backup process
            or deleted by the owner.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            This is a privately operated,
            single-user application.
        </p>

